cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this package, please cite it together with the evaluation article (see the article reference in the README)."
title: "mwi: Compute the Mosquito Weather Index"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22101143
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/E4Warning/mwi"
url: "https://e4warning.github.io/mwi/"
abstract: >-
  Computes the Mosquito Weather Index (MWI), an operational index combining air
  temperature, relative humidity and wind speed into a single number between 0
  and 1 summarising how favourable the weather is for adult mosquito activity,
  and maps that number onto five ordered activity classes. Developed by the
  Benaki Phytopathological Institute and the National Observatory of Athens
  under the LIFE CONOPS project (LIFE12 ENV/GR/000466).
